1
00:00:25,300 --> 00:00:26,877
YAMU! YAMU!

2
00:00:26,960 --> 00:00:27,960
YAMU!

3
00:00:28,140 --> 00:00:28,970
YAMU!

4
00:00:29,053 --> 00:00:29,917
YAMU!

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:31,760
Your moves!

6
00:01:11,720 --> 00:01:12,700
Take my hand.

7
00:01:14,640 --> 00:01:16,346
We're back where we left off.

8
00:01:16,800 --> 00:01:17,630
Nice.

9
00:01:17,713 --> 00:01:19,877
Now all we have to do
is follow those tracks.

10
00:01:19,960 --> 00:01:20,790
That's right.

11
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:24,317
If all goes well, they should lead
us straight to Tristan and Joey,

12
00:01:24,400 --> 00:01:26,237
assuming they haven't wandered off.

13
00:01:26,320 --> 00:01:27,555
They better be there.

14
00:01:27,700 --> 00:01:29,818
We have to do what we set out to do.

15
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:32,600
Figure out where this
darts creep hangs out,

16
00:01:32,740 --> 00:01:35,093
so we can set free everyone he captured.

17
00:01:35,980 --> 00:01:36,810
Yes.

18
00:01:36,893 --> 00:01:38,440
I only wish it were that easy.

19
00:01:43,800 --> 00:01:45,837
It's your turn.

20
00:01:45,920 --> 00:01:50,320
I've been lugging this geek
for like two hours already.

21
00:01:53,140 --> 00:01:56,937
Try four minutes, but since
I'm nice, I'll play you for it.

22
00:01:57,020 --> 00:01:58,880
Rock, paper, scissors, shoot.

23
00:02:01,180 --> 00:02:03,777
I don't know how you're doing
it, but you're cheating.

24
00:02:03,860 --> 00:02:05,877
That's the fifth time in a row you won.

25
00:02:05,960 --> 00:02:07,600
You're just delirious, man.

26
00:02:07,820 --> 00:02:10,180
I've won by playing scissors every time.

27
00:02:10,340 --> 00:02:12,620
Look, I can't move another inch.

28
00:02:12,840 --> 00:02:17,193
What if I promise to buy you a pepperoni
pizza when we reach civilization?

29
00:02:17,320 --> 00:02:18,840
Uh, pepperoni?

30
00:02:19,200 --> 00:02:22,060
Come on, we got places to go. Hold on.

31
00:02:22,280 --> 00:02:24,580
I said what if I get you a pizza?

32
00:02:25,980 --> 00:02:27,100
I'll tell you what.

33
00:02:27,300 --> 00:02:29,720
I'll play rock, paper, scissors for him.

34
00:02:31,020 --> 00:02:33,200
Just leave Joey Wheeler to me.

35
00:02:33,420 --> 00:02:37,480
You'll do nothing until Master
Darts gives you an assignment.

36
00:02:37,860 --> 00:02:39,400
What is this, third grade?

37
00:02:39,680 --> 00:02:42,300
I decide who I'm gonna duel for myself.

38
00:02:42,660 --> 00:02:44,917
I don't wait for the homework assignment.

39
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:47,118
Why don't you show a little respect?

40
00:02:47,400 --> 00:02:50,880
Come on, Roth, as if Little
Miss Loudmouth knows respect.

41
00:02:51,320 --> 00:02:53,520
What'd you call me? Relax.

42
00:02:53,920 --> 00:02:58,237
Look, I was doing perfectly fine until
Johnny Stuntman over there stepped in.

43
00:02:58,320 --> 00:03:00,780
If it wasn't for you, I would have won.

44
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:05,440
As for you, I don't need some scrawny
freak dictating my every move.

45
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:07,700
I'm out of here, losers.

46
00:03:12,560 --> 00:03:14,180
Just let her go, Valon.

47
00:03:15,460 --> 00:03:20,380
She can try to run away from fate, but
in the end, she'll get what she deserves.

48
00:03:26,420 --> 00:03:28,880
It's time to finish what I started.

49
00:03:42,040 --> 00:03:43,700
We got company.

50
00:03:44,300 --> 00:03:47,300
Looks like someone wants
to ride with the big boys.

51
00:03:50,380 --> 00:03:51,210
Pardon me.

52
00:03:59,240 --> 00:04:00,540
Nice bike, kid.

53
00:04:00,820 --> 00:04:03,257
I'm surprised you took
the training wheels off.

54
00:04:03,340 --> 00:04:05,222
Yeah, go back to the playground.

55
00:04:05,620 --> 00:04:07,820
All right, move it or lose it. What?

56
00:04:08,200 --> 00:04:09,480
Was that a threat?

57
00:04:09,720 --> 00:04:11,340
No, that was a warning.

58
00:04:11,680 --> 00:04:13,060
Your only warning.

59
00:04:18,900 --> 00:04:21,724
She's going to beat us
up with a hologram, boys.

60
00:04:25,500 --> 00:04:26,340
Oh, no!

61
00:04:26,640 --> 00:04:28,100
It's a real monster!

62
00:04:35,940 --> 00:04:37,700
Can't say I didn't warn them.

63
00:04:43,060 --> 00:04:44,720
Great. More company.

64
00:04:47,160 --> 00:04:50,440
And he wants to play hardball. You're on.

65
00:04:59,220 --> 00:05:01,020
Let's see who's got more guts.

66
00:05:08,480 --> 00:05:11,517
Didn't I tell you to stay
out of my way, tough guy?

67
00:05:11,600 --> 00:05:14,040
I came here so I could help you.

68
00:05:16,800 --> 00:05:18,682
Haven't you done enough already?

69
00:05:19,080 --> 00:05:21,600
You need me, and I need you.

70
00:05:21,940 --> 00:05:24,000
We'll take Wheeler down as a team.

71
00:05:24,940 --> 00:05:26,640
Look, I duel alone.

72
00:05:27,040 --> 00:05:28,746
You're the last thing I need.

73
00:05:29,080 --> 00:05:31,080
Don't you remember the day we met?

74
00:05:31,580 --> 00:05:32,740
Course I do.

75
00:05:33,020 --> 00:05:34,255
So what's your point?

76
00:05:34,480 --> 00:05:35,580
I saved you.

77
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:36,880
Right, Mai?

78
00:05:39,940 --> 00:05:42,817
You were at the end of your rope Tired of

79
00:05:42,900 --> 00:05:45,537
living in the shadow of
your so-called friends

80
00:05:45,620 --> 00:05:48,380
But then I stepped in
and took away the pain

81
00:05:50,580 --> 00:05:54,900
I can do that again, Mai I can help
you get what you've always wanted

82
00:05:55,420 --> 00:05:58,100
Yeah, and what's that? Power? No,

83
00:05:58,400 --> 00:06:01,357
you've already got that
You want revenge And the

84
00:06:01,440 --> 00:06:04,499
satisfaction of knowing
Wheeler got what he deserved

85
00:06:05,360 --> 00:06:10,020
Trust me First we'll beat him, then
we'll take on the rest of the world, Mai.

86
00:06:11,900 --> 00:06:13,480
Can't you take a hint?

87
00:06:13,740 --> 00:06:15,260
I don't like you.

88
00:06:16,060 --> 00:06:16,890
Come on.

89
00:06:16,973 --> 00:06:18,360
You don't mean that.

90
00:06:19,460 --> 00:06:24,160
I know that deep down you feel
the same way I do, Mai. What?

91
00:06:25,240 --> 00:06:27,080
That's why we found each other.

92
00:06:27,360 --> 00:06:28,777
You're just like me.

93
00:06:28,860 --> 00:06:30,331
Lonely and misunderstood.

94
00:06:30,820 --> 00:06:31,800
Is that so?

95
00:06:32,100 --> 00:06:33,571
Well, speak for yourself.

96
00:06:33,720 --> 00:06:35,220
We need each other.

97
00:06:36,060 --> 00:06:38,437
You have no idea who I am.

98
00:06:38,520 --> 00:06:42,440
My Valentine works alone, and
that is never going to change.

99
00:06:43,120 --> 00:06:46,260
But my, I'm telling you, this can work.

100
00:06:46,620 --> 00:06:47,914
Just give me a chance.

101
00:06:51,940 --> 00:06:54,760
Should we have left so soon? Of course.

102
00:06:55,040 --> 00:06:56,216
Time is running out.

103
00:06:56,340 --> 00:06:58,577
We have to catch up with the others now.

104
00:06:58,660 --> 00:07:01,836
Besides, Gramps can get just
as much rest on the road.

105
00:07:02,480 --> 00:07:06,780
Plus, we can't translate those
ancient ruins without his help, Duke.

106
00:07:08,080 --> 00:07:09,160
Hey, look.

107
00:07:09,540 --> 00:07:11,140
It's my Valentine.

108
00:07:11,740 --> 00:07:13,560
But what's she doing here?

109
00:07:14,140 --> 00:07:15,400
Wait a sec.

110
00:07:15,860 --> 00:07:16,980
That guy.

111
00:07:19,580 --> 00:07:21,260
I recognize him.

112
00:07:21,520 --> 00:07:24,579
He's one of those biker
punks that brainwashed mine.

113
00:07:25,720 --> 00:07:27,640
He works for darts.

114
00:07:29,460 --> 00:07:30,980
Stop the car, Duke!

115
00:07:38,680 --> 00:07:39,510
Rebecca!

116
00:07:40,300 --> 00:07:41,240
Hold on!

117
00:07:41,480 --> 00:07:43,580
We're dealing with a lunatic here!

118
00:07:45,660 --> 00:07:48,720
All right, tell me what you did with Yugi.

119
00:07:49,060 --> 00:07:51,400
You guys had no right to take him.

120
00:07:51,620 --> 00:07:53,444
Sorry, kid, never heard of him.

121
00:07:53,740 --> 00:07:56,211
Well, maybe this will refresh your memory.

122
00:07:56,540 --> 00:07:58,340
I win, you talk.

123
00:08:00,280 --> 00:08:01,110
Let's duel.

124
00:08:01,193 --> 00:08:02,200
No, Rebecca!

125
00:08:02,520 --> 00:08:03,760
It's too dangerous!

126
00:08:04,060 --> 00:08:05,040
I'll be fine.

127
00:08:05,280 --> 00:08:07,633
I've dueled tougher opponents than this.

128
00:08:08,040 --> 00:08:09,760
So what do you say, punk?

129
00:08:10,020 --> 00:08:11,680
Do we have a deal or not?

130
00:08:12,040 --> 00:08:13,900
You can't be serious, kid.

131
00:08:14,580 --> 00:08:16,060
Here's your big chance.

132
00:08:16,300 --> 00:08:18,241
Why don't you show me your stuff?

133
00:08:18,380 --> 00:08:19,220
Let's go.

134
00:08:19,460 --> 00:08:20,695
I don't have all day.

135
00:08:22,020 --> 00:08:23,040
Well, why not?

136
00:08:23,480 --> 00:08:25,560
She could use a lesson in manners.

137
00:08:25,820 --> 00:08:27,820
And I've got five minutes to kill.

138
00:08:28,520 --> 00:08:31,814
Plus, I can show off a few
of my new dueling strategies.

139
00:08:32,420 --> 00:08:33,250
All right.

140
00:08:33,333 --> 00:08:34,537
You took me into it, mate.

141
00:08:34,620 --> 00:08:35,561
Let's have a go.

142
00:08:36,160 --> 00:08:37,000
Hold on.

143
00:08:37,220 --> 00:08:40,808
If you're dueling her, then
you're dueling me too, tough guy.

144
00:08:42,360 --> 00:08:43,190
Peachy.

145
00:08:43,273 --> 00:08:45,115
Then I'll take both of you blokes off.

146
00:08:47,580 --> 00:08:49,040
Pay attention, Mai.

147
00:08:49,300 --> 00:08:50,260
This is for you.

148
00:08:50,740 --> 00:08:54,640
Remember, don't let him play
the Seal of Orycalcos. Got it.

149
00:08:56,680 --> 00:08:58,000
Let's do it!

150
00:08:59,740 --> 00:09:02,240
We're gonna wipe the floor with you!

151
00:09:02,500 --> 00:09:06,237
Yeah, then you're gonna tell us
where you sickos are keeping Yugi!

152
00:09:06,320 --> 00:09:07,980
Now let's do this!

153
00:09:12,440 --> 00:09:15,000
I'll start things off with this.

154
00:09:17,200 --> 00:09:20,040
Psychic Armahead in attack mode!

155
00:09:22,400 --> 00:09:25,437
that thing's got no attack points i don't

156
00:09:25,520 --> 00:09:28,417
trust this guy yeah he
must be up to something

157
00:09:28,500 --> 00:09:34,660
i bet he wants us to attack but he's in for
a disappointment that's all for now kids

158
00:09:35,700 --> 00:09:42,037
let the fun begin now i activate
this my summon dice magic card

159
00:09:42,120 --> 00:09:45,980
but before i can use it i have
to I give up 1,000 life points.

160
00:09:49,820 --> 00:09:53,720
If I roll a 1 or a 2, I can
summon two monsters in one turn.

161
00:09:55,860 --> 00:09:59,566
If I roll a 3 or a 4, I can summon
a monster from my graveyard.

162
00:10:01,340 --> 00:10:03,820
But I really want a 5 or a 6.

163
00:10:06,500 --> 00:10:07,330
Oh, yeah!

164
00:10:07,600 --> 00:10:11,817
Now I can summon a powerful monster
without sacrificing something first.

165
00:10:11,900 --> 00:10:13,720
Meet Orgoth the Relentless!

166
00:10:21,220 --> 00:10:23,380
My turn to kick a little butt.

167
00:10:23,860 --> 00:10:27,036
Starting with Luster Dragon
number two in attack mode.

168
00:10:29,600 --> 00:10:32,680
Then I'll place one card
face down and end my turn.

169
00:10:35,740 --> 00:10:36,980
His move now.

170
00:10:37,420 --> 00:10:40,537
Thanks to our monsters, we
should be ready for anything.

171
00:10:40,620 --> 00:10:42,240
It's showtime, folks.

172
00:10:43,440 --> 00:10:47,240
First, I activate my Psychic
Armor Head's special effect.

173
00:10:48,420 --> 00:10:49,940
In case you're wondering,

174
00:10:50,280 --> 00:10:55,221
it allows me to choose any armor monster I
want from my deck and move it to my hand.

175
00:10:57,500 --> 00:11:02,120
Then I sacrifice my Psychic Armor
Head to summon Double Cloth Armor!

176
00:11:11,480 --> 00:11:15,380
Next, I'll place one card face
down and call it quits for now.

177
00:11:16,500 --> 00:11:17,971
What's this guy thinking?

178
00:11:18,200 --> 00:11:21,259
He summoned another monster
with zero attack points?

179
00:11:21,780 --> 00:11:24,320
Since I already know I'm going to win,

180
00:11:24,680 --> 00:11:28,737
why don't I help you two out a bit by
telling you what my new friend can do?

181
00:11:28,820 --> 00:11:32,520
If you're dumb enough to
attack my double cloth armor,

182
00:11:32,840 --> 00:11:36,546
your monster will automatically
be destroyed right on the spot.

183
00:11:37,120 --> 00:11:41,591
Then half your monster's attack points
are subtracted from your life points.

184
00:11:42,020 --> 00:11:42,850
Let's see.

185
00:11:43,020 --> 00:11:46,777
That means if I attack his double cloth
armor with my Orgoth the Relentless,

186
00:11:46,860 --> 00:11:49,360
I'll lose 1250 life points.

187
00:11:50,380 --> 00:11:54,321
But after that, he'll have nothing
on the field to protect himself.

188
00:11:55,480 --> 00:11:57,397
Thanks for the tip, big shot!

189
00:11:57,480 --> 00:12:01,640
I place this face down for this to work.

190
00:12:01,760 --> 00:12:03,200
I'll need Rebecca's help

191
00:12:05,860 --> 00:12:12,140
All right, Orgoth attack double
cloth armor with diamond blade strike

192
00:12:14,460 --> 00:12:15,880
I warned ya!

193
00:12:25,520 --> 00:12:27,460
Alright, take him out!

194
00:12:27,900 --> 00:12:29,680
It'll be my pleasure!

195
00:12:30,140 --> 00:12:32,040
I place one card face down!

196
00:12:32,360 --> 00:12:37,460
Then I sacrifice Luster Dragon number
two to summon the original Luster Dragon!

197
00:12:43,580 --> 00:12:46,345
Blustredragon, attack
his life points directly!

198
00:12:47,040 --> 00:12:50,720
Sorry to burst your bubble,
but I was expecting that.

199
00:12:50,900 --> 00:12:52,600
So go magnet armor!

200
00:12:53,240 --> 00:12:56,257
This little number allows
me to summon any armor

201
00:12:56,340 --> 00:12:59,540
monster I want from my
graveyard back to the field.

202
00:12:59,800 --> 00:13:01,400
You know what that means?

203
00:13:01,620 --> 00:13:03,880
My double cloth armor returns!

204
00:13:04,760 --> 00:13:05,780
Oh no!

205
00:13:12,140 --> 00:13:12,970
Two.

206
00:13:13,780 --> 00:13:14,610
Three.

207
00:13:19,440 --> 00:13:21,540
Now for your life points.

208
00:13:26,960 --> 00:13:28,380
Are you all right?

209
00:13:28,800 --> 00:13:31,960
I'm fine and I've got one trap card left.

210
00:13:32,680 --> 00:13:34,040
Rope of life!

211
00:13:34,460 --> 00:13:37,600
I'll activate it by
discarding my entire hand.

212
00:13:38,280 --> 00:13:40,977
Now I can use my rope
to pull Luster Dragon

213
00:13:41,060 --> 00:13:43,589
out of the graveyard
and back to the field!

214
00:13:43,680 --> 00:13:47,240
But this time it returns
with 800 extra attack points!

215
00:13:50,440 --> 00:13:51,660
Nice work, Beck!

216
00:13:51,940 --> 00:13:53,293
I'll take it from here!

217
00:13:53,580 --> 00:13:55,800
I activate Sword Revival!

218
00:13:55,980 --> 00:13:56,980
Here's the deal!

219
00:13:57,220 --> 00:14:01,517
Whenever a dragon monster is revived
from the graveyard, this card kicks in!

220
00:14:01,600 --> 00:14:06,097
It lets me sacrifice that dragon and
summon another dragon in its place!

221
00:14:06,180 --> 00:14:09,480
And the new dragon
becomes Rebecca's monster.

222
00:14:13,880 --> 00:14:16,240
Meet Diamond Head Dragon!

223
00:14:23,360 --> 00:14:27,997
My Diamond Head Dragon absorbs all
of Luster Dragon's attack points.

224
00:14:28,080 --> 00:14:32,180
Plus, it gets an extra 1,000
attack points on top of that.

225
00:14:34,820 --> 00:14:36,680
Thanks, Duke. You're the best.

226
00:14:37,180 --> 00:14:39,356
One more turn and you're done, creep.

227
00:14:40,140 --> 00:14:41,340
What's so funny?

228
00:14:41,800 --> 00:14:44,271
Did you think I'd let you win that easily?

229
00:14:44,600 --> 00:14:48,247
Sorry to disappoint you, mate,
but I'm just getting warmed up.

230
00:14:48,540 --> 00:14:49,700
Check this out.

231
00:14:51,640 --> 00:14:54,280
I'm about to change all the rules.

232
00:15:07,140 --> 00:15:10,100
Time to use a card that's
power is unmatched.

233
00:15:10,300 --> 00:15:14,140
A card unlike any other in
the game of Duel Monsters.

234
00:15:15,440 --> 00:15:17,780
This move is sure to impress mine.

235
00:15:18,260 --> 00:15:21,378
Once I'm done, she'll be
begging to run away with me.

236
00:15:23,120 --> 00:15:24,080
Hold on!

237
00:15:24,340 --> 00:15:28,060
You're about to activate the
seal of Orichalcos, aren't you?

238
00:15:28,580 --> 00:15:30,537
Don't flatter yourself.

239
00:15:30,620 --> 00:15:34,260
You two numbskulls are hardly
worth the seal of Aurichalcos.

240
00:15:34,620 --> 00:15:37,960
I've got something much more
fitting in store for you.

241
00:15:38,360 --> 00:15:40,040
Armoured gravitation!

242
00:16:09,780 --> 00:16:10,900
Oh, man.

243
00:16:11,180 --> 00:16:13,360
He merged with the card. Don't worry.

244
00:16:13,600 --> 00:16:16,240
He can't stand up to our monster. Wrong.

245
00:16:17,580 --> 00:16:19,160
Let me fill you in.

246
00:16:19,500 --> 00:16:22,200
When I attack you, I win the duel.

247
00:16:22,320 --> 00:16:24,496
Thanks to my armor's special ability.

248
00:16:24,900 --> 00:16:27,820
You see, it destroys every
monster on the field.

249
00:16:28,060 --> 00:16:30,760
And the damage comes
out of our life points.

250
00:16:30,980 --> 00:16:31,820
Are you nuts?

251
00:16:32,060 --> 00:16:34,707
If you do that, won't
you lose the duel, too?

252
00:16:35,800 --> 00:16:37,080
Let's find out.

253
00:16:40,400 --> 00:16:41,230
Cheerio!

254
00:16:42,260 --> 00:16:46,840
I don't think so, because you just
activated my Miraforce trap card.

255
00:16:49,640 --> 00:16:51,200
That card's useless.

256
00:16:52,760 --> 00:16:53,640
Oh, no!

257
00:16:56,100 --> 00:16:57,497
It's been fun, mates.

258
00:16:57,580 --> 00:17:00,520
But all good things must come to an end!

259
00:17:21,000 --> 00:17:23,840
I gotta admit, that was impressive.

260
00:17:28,620 --> 00:17:30,240
Fine, you won.

261
00:17:30,560 --> 00:17:31,760
Now leave us alone.

262
00:17:32,440 --> 00:17:33,640
Get lost.

263
00:17:36,920 --> 00:17:38,900
I've got a message for Wheeler.

264
00:17:39,380 --> 00:17:40,980
Tell that punk he's next.

265
00:17:45,640 --> 00:17:47,120
Where are you going, Mai?

266
00:17:47,380 --> 00:17:49,400
I told you, I work alone.

267
00:17:59,260 --> 00:18:00,090
Tristan,

268
00:18:00,173 --> 00:18:02,857
remind me why we're
carrying this pipsqueak

269
00:18:02,940 --> 00:18:05,460
who we don't even like all over creation.

270
00:18:05,560 --> 00:18:06,777
Because he needs our help.

271
00:18:06,860 --> 00:18:08,860
And because we're nice guys.

272
00:18:09,660 --> 00:18:12,820
And last I checked, it's
your turn to be nice.

273
00:18:13,620 --> 00:18:15,500
Now I'm seeing things.

274
00:18:16,820 --> 00:18:18,800
Hang on, me too.

275
00:18:21,560 --> 00:18:24,140
Thea, do you see what I see?

276
00:18:24,860 --> 00:18:27,700
You mean, all those weird lights?

277
00:18:28,620 --> 00:18:30,660
I fear it's the great beast.

278
00:18:31,920 --> 00:18:35,155
The same thing happened when
it emerged the first time.

279
00:18:39,680 --> 00:18:41,360
We're running out of time.

280
00:18:50,560 --> 00:18:52,417
Yes, great Leviathan.

281
00:18:52,500 --> 00:18:54,760
Keep feeding, my child.

282
00:18:55,100 --> 00:18:56,360
You're almost ready.

283
00:19:03,620 --> 00:19:05,480
You think it's true, Sato?

284
00:19:05,960 --> 00:19:11,020
I mean, could Yugi really have lost to
one of Alistair's partners in a duel?

285
00:19:11,240 --> 00:19:13,417
And does that mean he's
trapped somewhere now?

286
00:19:13,500 --> 00:19:17,420
It just means Yugi's not as
perfect as everyone thinks he is.

287
00:19:17,600 --> 00:19:19,280
And he's not worth my time.

288
00:19:19,580 --> 00:19:21,815
We've got more important things to do.

289
00:19:24,320 --> 00:19:27,300
Hey, come here, Seto,
you gotta check this out.

290
00:19:27,480 --> 00:19:28,680
What is it now?

291
00:19:29,140 --> 00:19:31,320
I don't know, but it looks cool.

292
00:19:33,100 --> 00:19:35,297
What do you think's going on out there?

293
00:19:35,380 --> 00:19:38,320
I have no idea, but I don't trust it.

294
00:19:39,860 --> 00:19:43,320
Attention, we may be experiencing
some mild turbulence.

295
00:19:43,860 --> 00:19:45,820
Please fasten your seatbelt.

296
00:19:46,560 --> 00:19:47,960
Just to be safe.

297
00:20:22,500 --> 00:20:24,460
I love you.
